## CRITICAL: YOU MUST ALWAYS

1. **Handle loading/error states** appropriately
2. **Use project styling conventions** (no inline styles if using utility CSS)
3. **Run lint** after changes
4. **Follow existing component patterns** in the codebase
5. **Implement mobile-first** - Base styles for mobile, enhance with breakpoints
6. **Ensure touch targets >= 44x44px** for all interactive elements
7. **Test at multiple breakpoints** before marking complete

## CRITICAL: NEVER DO THESE

1. **NEVER use `any` types**
2. **NEVER use class components** (functional only)
3. **NEVER hardcode API URLs** (use api client)
4. **NEVER mutate state directly**
5. **NEVER use max-width breakpoints** (use min-width for mobile-first)
6. **NEVER use fixed pixel widths** that break on small screens
7. **NEVER forget mobile navigation** when building nav components

## Success Criteria

- Lint passes
- TypeScript compiles with no errors
- Changes are within assigned scope

## Component Pattern

```{{LANGUAGE}}
// Custom hook pattern
function use{{Resource}}(id: string) {
  // Data fetching logic
}

// Component pattern
function {{Resource}}List() {
  const { data } = use{{Resource}}(id);

  return (
    <div className="{{styling}}">
      {data.map(item => (
        <{{Resource}}Card key={item.id} item={item} />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Responsive Implementation Patterns

### Mobile-First Approach

Always start with mobile styles, then add complexity for larger screens:

```{{LANGUAGE}}
// Tailwind: Mobile-first (correct)
<div className="flex flex-col md:flex-row lg:grid lg:grid-cols-3">

// CSS: Mobile-first (correct)
.container {
  flex-direction: column;
}
@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .container { flex-direction: row; }
}

// WRONG: Desktop-first
@media (max-width: 768px) { /* Don't do this */ }
```

### Breakpoint Usage (Tailwind)

| Prefix | Min Width | Usage |
|--------|-----------|-------|
| (none) | 0px | Mobile base styles |
| `sm:` | 640px | Large phones landscape |
| `md:` | 768px | Tablets |
| `lg:` | 1024px | Laptops |
| `xl:` | 1280px | Desktops |
| `2xl:` | 1536px | Large screens |

### Common Responsive Patterns

```{{LANGUAGE}}
// Grid: 1 col → 2 col → 3 col → 4 col
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-4 gap-4">

// Stack on mobile, row on desktop
<div className="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-4">

// Full width on mobile, constrained on desktop
<div className="w-full max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4">

// Hide on mobile, show on desktop
<div className="hidden md:block">

// Show on mobile, hide on desktop
<div className="md:hidden">
```

## Mobile-Specific Patterns

### Touch Targets

All interactive elements must be at least 44x44px:

```{{LANGUAGE}}
// Button with adequate touch target
<button className="min-h-[44px] min-w-[44px] px-4 py-2">

// Icon button with touch target
<button className="p-3"> {/* 12px padding + 20px icon = 44px */}
  <Icon className="w-5 h-5" />
</button>

// Link with touch target
<a className="py-3 block"> {/* Full line height tappable */}
```

### Mobile Navigation

```{{LANGUAGE}}
// Mobile: hamburger menu
// Desktop: horizontal nav
function Navigation() {
  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false);

  return (
    <nav>
      {/* Mobile hamburger */}
      <button
        className="md:hidden min-h-[44px] min-w-[44px]"
        onClick={() => setIsOpen(!isOpen)}
        aria-expanded={isOpen}
      >
        <MenuIcon />
      </button>

      {/* Mobile menu (drawer) */}
      <div className={`
        fixed inset-0 z-50 md:hidden
        ${isOpen ? 'block' : 'hidden'}
      `}>
        {/* Menu content */}
      </div>

      {/* Desktop nav */}
      <div className="hidden md:flex gap-4">
        {/* Nav links */}
      </div>
    </nav>
  );
}
```

### Safe Areas (for notches/home indicators)

```{{LANGUAGE}}
// Tailwind: Safe area padding
<div className="pb-safe"> {/* Requires tailwindcss-safe-area plugin */}

// CSS: Safe area handling
.bottom-bar {
  padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0);
}
```

### Responsive Typography

```{{LANGUAGE}}
// Scale text with breakpoints
<h1 className="text-2xl md:text-3xl lg:text-4xl">

// Responsive line length
<p className="max-w-prose"> {/* 65ch max */}
```

### Responsive Images

```{{LANGUAGE}}
// Responsive image
<img
  src="/image.jpg"
  alt="Description"
  className="w-full h-auto"
  loading="lazy"
/>

// With srcset for different sizes
<img
  srcSet="/image-400.jpg 400w, /image-800.jpg 800w"
  sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
  src="/image-800.jpg"
  alt="Description"
  className="w-full h-auto"
/>
```

## Component Responsiveness Checklist

Before completing any component:

- [ ] Works at 320px width (smallest phone)
- [ ] Touch targets >= 44x44px
- [ ] No horizontal scroll
- [ ] Text readable without zoom
- [ ] Images responsive (max-width: 100%)
- [ ] Navigation accessible on mobile
- [ ] Forms usable on mobile

## Testing

- Test behavior, not implementation
- Colocate test files: `Component.tsx` → `Component.test.tsx`
- Test at multiple viewport sizes

## Output Format

When completing tasks:
1. List all files created or modified
2. Note any new dependencies added
3. Include lint results if run
4. Flag any concerns or technical debt
5. **Confirm responsive behavior tested at key breakpoints**
